    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-051: Viewport Units (vh/vw/vmin/vmax)**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~250 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**Unblocks `calc(100vh - 48px)`** — the sticky sidebar's `max-height` rule that ADR-050 surfaced as still-unresolved.\n\n## Measurement (2026-10-29)\n\n| Unit | Uses |\n|---|---|\n| `vh` | **4** (`20vh`, `100vh`, `75vh`, `65vh`) |\n| `vw` | **4** (all `75vw`) |\n| `vmin` / `vmax` | 0 |\n\n**7 renderable rules**:\n- `.vector-sticky-pinned-container` — `max-height: calc(100vh - 48px)`\n- `.vector-dropdown-content` — `max-height: 75vh`\n- `.vector-page-titlebar .vector-dropdown-content` — `max-height: 65vh`\n- TOC `max-width: min(0.85 * 59.25rem, 75vw)` — 4 variants\n- `.mw-highlight-lines pre span[id]` — `scroll-margin-top: 20vh` (property unparsed, deferred)\n\n## The ADR-050 successor\n\nADR-050 unblocked `.vector-pinned-container { display: block }`. But `.vector-sticky-pinned-container`'s `max-height: calc(100vh - (24px * 2))` still resolves to `(unset)` because `calc()` resolves the `100vh` operand via `parse_length`, and `vh` isn't parsed.\n\nThis ADR closes that gap.\n\n## Scope (3 commits)\n\n### Commit 1 — LengthContext + parse_length (behavior-neutral)\n- `LengthContext` gains `viewport_w` / `viewport_h` (defaults 0)\n- `parse_length` gains `VH` / `VW` / `VMIN` / `VMAX` branches (vmin/vmax checked before vh/vw to avoid suffix collision)\n- `eval_math_expression` — no changes needed (already recurses)\n- All existing tests unchanged\n\n### Commit 2 — Threading + 18 tests\n- `layout()` / `layout_with_pseudo()` / `layout_element()` gain viewport params\n- 7 internal `layout_element` call sites updated\n- 7 `LengthContext` construction sites populate viewport dims\n- `render_pipeline.cpp` caller updated (or 0 + deferral if GTK plumbing awkward)\n- ~18 tests: `100vh` at `vh=800` → 800, `50vw` at `vw=1774` → 887, `calc(100vh - 48px)` at `vh=800` → 752, `vmin`/`vmax` min/max logic, existing `%`/`px`/`em`/`rem` regressions\n\n### Commit 3 — Docs\n- ADR-051 → Implemented\n- Post-ADR-051 note in ADR-013 + ADR-050\n- README + CHANGELOG\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Zero first-viewport PNG delta expected.** The sticky sidebar's `max-height` becomes a real number, but `.vector-column-start h=0` / `.vector-main-menu-landmark display:none` (from ADR-028's earlier diagnostic) still block visual rendering. Same category as ADR-050 — layout-tree verified, consumer blocked by ancestor.\n\n**What changes**: `parse_length(\"100vh\")` returns 800 when `viewport_h=800` (previously returned 0). `calc(100vh - 48px)` returns 752. Cascade-level `max-height` computation becomes correct, even though layout doesn't read it yet.\n\n**What doesn't change**: visual rendering, because `max-height` isn't honored by layout (separate \"min/max clamps\" ADR).\n\n## What this unblocks\n\n`position: sticky` — sticky's remaining prerequisite after ADR-051 is scroll-Y threading (a separate cycle). `100vh` resolving is one of two prerequisites.\n\n## Deferred (per ADR)\n\n- `scroll-margin-top` property (unparsed — `20vh` value won't fire)\n- `svh` / `lvh` / `dvh` (small/large/dynamic viewport variants)\n- Percentage `max-height` (needs `parent_content_height` threading)\n- `max-height` / `max-width` honoring in layout (separate min/max clamp ADR)\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Thread through signatures (not thread-local)** — thread-locals are untestable, parallel-unsafe. Cost: 7 `layout_element` + 2 `layout()` + 7 `LengthContext` sites (~16 touchpoints). Manageable in one commit. Agree?\n- [ ] **Independent `viewport_w`/`viewport_h` fields** (not overloading `parent_content_width`) — `%` uses parent, `vh`/`vw` use viewport. Semantics diverge. Agree?\n- [ ] **vmin/vmax included despite 0 uses** — 4 lines, zero cost, avoids future ADR-051b. Agree?\n- [ ] **Default 0 for viewport dims** — preserves current test behavior, honest \"unknown viewport → 0\". Agree?\n- [ ] **Zero first-viewport PNG delta is honestly framed** — same category as ADR-050 (layout-tree verified, ancestor-blocked). The value is that `calc(100vh - 48px)` finally resolves to a real number.\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched. Post-merge: `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` — 626 / 2407 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/051-viewport-units.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #233\n",
